      "content": "A more nuanced approach acknowledges the tension between presidential privilege and congressional oversight. You can adopt a balanced perspective that considers both sides and argues that while executive privilege does provide necessary protection for confidential communications, its expansion can indeed threaten the delicate balance of power. This stance can be fortified by comparing it to other areas of law, such as attorney-client privilege, where reasonable secrecy is not only protected but also recognized as a necessary component of the attorney-client relationship.",
      "source": "target",
