      "content": "i get the \"nuanced\" thing, but that's kind of a cop-out for a moot court. if i'm in front of a judge, they don't want a \"both sides\" answer, they want a killer argument. \n\nlook, you already said you lean towards the side of protecting the presidency. if you really think the expansion of privilege is a \"necessary protection,\" then help me double down on that. specifically, if a judge pushes back and says that the principle of \"transparency in a democracy\" outweighs any need for executive secrecy, what is the definitive legal rebuttal that proves the privilege side is actually the more constitutionally sound position? give me the shot that wins the round.",
