      "content": "In response to the judge's query about the tension between executive privilege and transparency, you can cite the Marbury v. Madison (1803) precedent, which established the Supreme Court's power to review executive actions. By extension, you can argue that any president who invokes privilege must demonstrate that a constitutional or statutory duty to disclose information has been violated, effectively forcing the executive to shed secrecy in favor of transparency or justification under law. This approach not only defends executive privilege but also firmly upholds the constitutional framework that governs government accountability.",
